    brutal mode update and cycle guitar fx strings
    
    This commit updates the brutal mode modifier to be more like the one
    found in Rock Band 4. It also adds visual feedback to the "cycle
    guitar FX" setting, even though I currently think that function is
    broken on HMX's side.
    
    Files this commit touches:
    
    dx/game/dx_game_funcs.dta
    These changes call the brutal mode func in dx_add_player_sinks (which
    should set each slot to the starting value).
    
    dx/game/dx_game_handles.dta
    These changes call brutal mode func from dx_on_game_enter and
    dx_on_game_reset (not sure if both this and the above are needed, but
    it works).
    
    dx/locale/locale_updates.dta
    These additions are for the updates to the cycle guitar fx setting.
    
    dx/overshell/dx_main_states.dta
    These changes rotate through strings for the cycle guitar fx function.
    
    dx/track/beatmatch/dx_beatmatch_funcs.dta
    These changes repurpose the timer debug option for the brutal mode
    numbers as well as the "cooked" crowd meter for each slot.
    
    dx/track/callbacks/dx_track_callback_funcs.dta
    These changes are the meat of the updated brutal mode. The old one is
    still present for the moment, and could be re-added as an option if
    a player prefers jnack's original implementation. It adds the following
    functions:
    dx_cook_crowd - converts raw crowd rating to the range 0.0-1.0
    dx_get_brutal_number_dx - this was my original implementation without
                              the ranges
    dx_get_brutal_number_rb4 - this function returns the proper bottom_y
                               based on the range of crowd meter position
    dx_brutal_mode - a springboard function to avoid renaming every call
                     of this function, and also allows for future variations
                     on brutal mode to be selectable
    dx_brutal_mode_dx - my original naive mapping of crowd meter to brutal
                        position
    dx_brutal_mode_rb4_new - this is the one I tried to use one singular
                             func to build the proper variable and symbol
                             names, I was unable to get it to work but I
                             want to revisit it in the future
    dx_brutal_mode_rb4 - this is the meat of the function, that updates
                         the bottom_y for each track and also positions
                         the label, deleting it first if necessary. also
                         ensures the labels and colors are deleted if
                         brutal mode is disabled after one or more songs
                         with brutal mode on
    dx_brutal_mode_jnack - jnack's original brutal mode implementation
    
    dx/ui/dx_ui_init.dta
    These changes reset the "brutal mode initialized" var for each slot,
    which ensures I don't accidentally create too many labels. It also
    resets the counter used by the next file's changes.
    
    ui/game.dta - adds a tiny amount of script to the beat handler to
                  attempt to call the dx_brutal_mode script with a dummy
                  argument (since the new function doesn't really take
                  an argument but the original one does, and I wanted
                  us to be able to switch between them in the future),
                  this doesn't seem to work but I still need to figure
                  out how to get bottom_y set up before the first note
    
    This script *should* work in multiplayer, possibly online too? If
    anyone notices any bugs, please file an issue. I tested this for
    the brunt of four hours on stream today, playing on guitar, and it
    worked without issue.

